From f20efc56ece0147b846fa331122ee3f0785f420f Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Ian Blenke <ian@blenke.com>
Date: Wed, 1 Jul 2026 19:36:11 -0400
Subject: [PATCH 05371/11362] [outer-loop] make retired scopes load-bearing at
 activation: BLOCKED_PATTERN_MATCHED class

Direct follow-up to the operator's chosen fix: 'fix #1 mechanically, not
as a standing outer-loop power.'

Root cause investigation: .469's planner ran 8 minutes AFTER a same-session
known-issues.md retraction landed (the FoVer in-domain candidate-selection-
pool premise) but still emitted 3 tasks asserting it as fact. Traced why
neither of scripts/exclusion_manifest_lint.py's existing violation classes
would have caught it: EXP_ID_RETIRED only matches a task id that REUSES a
retired id (these were brand-new ids); SCOPE_MATCHED_PRIOR_FAILURE's
FailureLedger only matches a task's scope-signature against PAST
ARTIFACTS' verdicts (no prior artifact existed for these ids at planning
time). Separately discovered ops/exclusion_manifest.yaml's
retired_extras[].blocked_patterns field -- free-text scope descriptions
written by past retirement-reporting scripts -- was pure documentation:
nothing in the live activation path ever read it.

Added a 5th violation class, BLOCKED_PATTERN_MATCHED: every draft task's
title+prompt is checked against every blocked_patterns entry across the
manifest, independent of the task's own id or artifact history. Same
override semantics as SCOPE_MATCHED_PRIOR_FAILURE (valid prior_failures:
clears the check; operator_override: downgrades HARD to WARNING). Added
a proper retired_extras entry for the FoVer in-domain retraction itself
so the specific incident is now mechanically covered too.

Verified end-to-end against synthetic roadmaps: matched-and-blocked,
matched-with-override (WARNING, passes), matched-with-valid-prior_failures
(clears entirely), and unrelated-clean, plus a regression check that the
currently-active research-roadmap.yaml still lints clean. 6 new tests in
tests/python/test_exclusion_manifest_lint.py, all passing. Also corrected
a stale CLAUDE.md paragraph that described exclusion_manifest_lint.py as
future work when it has been shipped and wired into
_activate_next_roadmap() since 2026-05-17.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Sonnet 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
